  31:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Initialize the CAN low level resources by implementing the
ARM GAS  /var/folders/8x/_y6g3dfs0698dfd49y4vcg_w0000gn/T//ccYyxujy.s 			page 2


  32:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_MspInit():
  33:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****          (++) Enable the CAN interface clock using __HAL_RCC_CANx_CLK_ENABLE()
  34:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****          (++) Configure CAN pins
  35:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****              (+++) Enable the clock for the CAN GPIOs
  36:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****              (+++) Configure CAN pins as alternate function
  37:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****          (++) In case of using interrupts (e.g. HAL_CAN_ActivateNotification())
  38:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****              (+++) Configure the CAN interrupt priority using
  39:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                    HAL_NVIC_SetPriority()
  40:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****              (+++) Enable the CAN IRQ handler using HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ()
  41:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****              (+++) In CAN IRQ handler, call HAL_CAN_IRQHandler()
  42:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
  43:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Initialize the CAN peripheral using HAL_CAN_Init() function. This
  44:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           function resorts to HAL_CAN_MspInit() for low-level initialization.
  45:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
  46:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Configure the reception filters using the following configuration
  47:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           functions:
  48:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) HAL_CAN_ConfigFilter()
  49:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
  50:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Start the CAN module using HAL_CAN_Start() function. At this level
  51:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           the node is active on the bus: it receive messages, and can send
  52:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           messages.
  53:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
  54:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) To manage messages transmission, the following Tx control functions
  55:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           can be used:
  56:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) HAL_CAN_AddTxMessage() to request transmission of a new
  57:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  message.
  58:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) HAL_CAN_AbortTxRequest() to abort transmission of a pending
  59:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  message.
  60:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) HAL_CAN_GetTxMailboxesFreeLevel() to get the number of free Tx
  61:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  mailboxes.
  62:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) HAL_CAN_IsTxMessagePending() to check if a message is pending
  63:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  in a Tx mailbox.
  64:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) HAL_CAN_GetTxTimestamp() to get the timestamp of Tx message
  65:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  sent, if time triggered communication mode is enabled.
  66:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
  67:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) When a message is received into the CAN Rx FIFOs, it can be retrieved
  68:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           using the HAL_CAN_GetRxMessage() function. The function
  69:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_GetRxFifoFillLevel() allows to know how many Rx message are
  70:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           stored in the Rx Fifo.
  71:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
  72:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Calling the HAL_CAN_Stop() function stops the CAN module.
  73:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
  74:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) The deinitialization is achieved with HAL_CAN_DeInit() function.
  75:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
  76:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
  77:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       *** Polling mode operation ***
  78:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       ==============================
  79:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     [..]
  80:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Reception:
  81:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Monitor reception of message using HAL_CAN_GetRxFifoFillLevel()
  82:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  until at least one message is received.
  83:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Then get the message using HAL_CAN_GetRxMessage().
  84:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
  85:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Transmission:
  86:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Monitor the Tx mailboxes availability until at least one Tx
  87:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  mailbox is free, using HAL_CAN_GetTxMailboxesFreeLevel().
  88:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Then request transmission of a message using
ARM GAS  /var/folders/8x/_y6g3dfs0698dfd49y4vcg_w0000gn/T//ccYyxujy.s 			page 3


  89:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  HAL_CAN_AddTxMessage().
  90:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
  91:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
  92:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       *** Interrupt mode operation ***
  93:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       ================================
  94:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     [..]
  95:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Notifications are activated using HAL_CAN_ActivateNotification()
  96:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           function. Then, the process can be controlled through the
  97:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           available user callbacks: HAL_CAN_xxxCallback(), using same APIs
  98:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_GetRxMessage() and HAL_CAN_AddTxMessage().
  99:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
 100:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Notifications can be deactivated using
 101:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_DeactivateNotification() function.
 102:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
 103:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) Special care should be taken for CAN_IT_RX_FIFO0_MSG_PENDING and
 104:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           CAN_IT_RX_FIFO1_MSG_PENDING notifications. These notifications trig
 105:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           the callbacks HAL_CAN_RxFIFO0MsgPendingCallback() and
 106:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_RxFIFO1MsgPendingCallback(). User has two possible options
 107:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           here.
 108:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Directly get the Rx message in the callback, using
 109:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  HAL_CAN_GetRxMessage().
 110:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Or deactivate the notification in the callback without
 111:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  getting the Rx message. The Rx message can then be got later
 112:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  using HAL_CAN_GetRxMessage(). Once the Rx message have been
 113:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  read, the notification can be activated again.
 114:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
 115:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
 116:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       *** Sleep mode ***
 117:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       ==================
 118:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     [..]
 119:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) The CAN peripheral can be put in sleep mode (low power), using
 120:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_RequestSleep(). The sleep mode will be entered as soon as the
 121:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           current CAN activity (transmission or reception of a CAN frame) will
 122:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           be completed.
 123:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
 124:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) A notification can be activated to be informed when the sleep mode
 125:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           will be entered.
 126:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
 127:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) It can be checked if the sleep mode is entered using
 128:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_IsSleepActive().
 129:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           Note that the CAN state (accessible from the API HAL_CAN_GetState())
 130:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           is HAL_CAN_STATE_SLEEP_PENDING as soon as the sleep mode request is
 131:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           submitted (the sleep mode is not yet entered), and become
 132:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****           HAL_CAN_STATE_SLEEP_ACTIVE when the sleep mode is effective.
 133:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
 134:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****       (#) The wake-up from sleep mode can be triggered by two ways:
 135:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) Using HAL_CAN_WakeUp(). When returning from this function,
 136:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  the sleep mode is exited (if return status is HAL_OK).
 137:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****             (++) When a start of Rx CAN frame is detected by the CAN peripheral,
 138:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****                  if automatic wake up mode is enabled.
 139:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
 140:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   *** Callback registration ***
 141:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   =============================================
 142:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
 143:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   The compilation define  USE_HAL_CAN_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
 144:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
 145:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   Use Function HAL_CAN_RegisterCallback() to register an interrupt callback.
ARM GAS  /var/folders/8x/_y6g3dfs0698dfd49y4vcg_w0000gn/T//ccYyxujy.s 			page 4


 146:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
 147:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   Function HAL_CAN_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
 148:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox0CompleteCallback   : Tx Mailbox 0 Complete Callback.
 149:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox1CompleteCallback   : Tx Mailbox 1 Complete Callback.
 150:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox2CompleteCallback   : Tx Mailbox 2 Complete Callback.
 151:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox0AbortCallback      : Tx Mailbox 0 Abort Callback.
 152:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox1AbortCallback      : Tx Mailbox 1 Abort Callback.
 153:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox2AbortCallback      : Tx Mailbox 2 Abort Callback.
 154:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) RxFifo0MsgPendingCallback    : Rx Fifo 0 Message Pending Callback.
 155:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) RxFifo0FullCallback          : Rx Fifo 0 Full Callback.
 156:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) RxFifo1MsgPendingCallback    : Rx Fifo 1 Message Pending Callback.
 157:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) RxFifo1FullCallback          : Rx Fifo 1 Full Callback.
 158:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) SleepCallback                : Sleep Callback.
 159:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) WakeUpFromRxMsgCallback      : Wake Up From Rx Message Callback.
 160:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) ErrorCallback                : Error Callback.
 161:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) MspInitCallback              : CAN MspInit.
 162:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) MspDeInitCallback            : CAN MspDeInit.
 163:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
 164:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   and a pointer to the user callback function.
 165:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
 166:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   Use function HAL_CAN_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to the default
 167:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   weak function.
 168:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   HAL_CAN_UnRegisterCallback takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
 169:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   and the Callback ID.
 170:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   This function allows to reset following callbacks:
 171:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox0CompleteCallback   : Tx Mailbox 0 Complete Callback.
 172:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox1CompleteCallback   : Tx Mailbox 1 Complete Callback.
 173:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****     (+) TxMailbox2CompleteCallback   : Tx Mailbox 2 Complete Callback.
