 187:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   By default, after the HAL_CAN_Init() and when the state is HAL_CAN_STATE_RESET,
 188:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak functions:
 189:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   example HAL_CAN_ErrorCallback().
 190:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are
 191:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   reset to the legacy weak function in the HAL_CAN_Init()/ HAL_CAN_DeInit() only when
 192:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 193:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   if not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_CAN_Init()/ HAL_CAN_DeInit()
 194:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand)
 195:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c **** 
 196:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in HAL_CAN_STATE_READY state only.
 197:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   Exception done MspInit/MspDeInit that can be registered/unregistered
 198:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   in HAL_CAN_STATE_READY or HAL_CAN_STATE_RESET state,
 199:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   thus registered (user) MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init/DeInit.
 200:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 201:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   using HAL_CAN_RegisterCallback() before calling HAL_CAN_DeInit()
 202:Drivers/STM32F2xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f2xx_hal_can.c ****   or HAL_CAN_Init() function.
